The '''540 Kick''' is a technique used in [[tricking]]. The name refers to a spin of approximately 540 degrees, accompanied by either a roundhouse or crescent kick. The same leg is used for the takeoff, kick and landing while the other is mainly used for momentum. It is often accompanied by a spin either before or after the kick.

