[[File:Muscle-up.jpg|thumb]]
A '''Muscle Up''' is an exercise in which one goes from a overhand pull-up position to a cast position (where the bar is at the waist). It can be performed on rings, a branch, a bar, or any sturdy surface that's easy to hang from. Although it is most commonly used as an exercise (since the [[bar kip]] is easier to use), it is occasionally used in [[Parkour]] as there are places were both a [[climb up]] and a bar kip would be impossible (such as under an overhanging ledge).

{{Infobox technique
|image = 
|discipline = [[Freerunning]]
|difficulty = Intermediate
}}
The '''Palm Flip''' is a [[wall flip]] used in [[freerunning]] where the practioner runs towards a wall and then pushes off the wall to rotate themselves backward directly into a [[back flip]]. One or more [[wallrun|steps]] can also be added before the flip for added height.

{{Infobox technique
|image = Parkour_Rail_Flip_2_by_Rusty_Photos.jpg
|discipline = [[Freerunning]]
|difficulty = Intermediate
}}
A '''Rail Flip''' is a [[vault]] used in [[freerunning]] where two hands are placed on top of an obstacle and a [[front handspring]] is executed to get over it. This move may also be started with a dive.

{{Infobox technique
|image = 370790160 340b641f1d.jpg
|discipline = [[Freerunning]]
|difficulty = Basic
}}
The '''Rocket Vault''' is a [[vault]] used in [[freerunning]] where the practitioner moves in a [[lazy vault]] fashion but both legs are brought together perfectly straight and the feet are grabbed by their hand and is held above their head at a 45 degree angle.

{{Infobox technique
|image = 
|discipline = [[Parkour]]
|difficulty = Beginner
}}
The '''Safety Vault''' is a  [[vault]] used in [[parkour]] that is much easier variation of the [[side vault]], except the the outside foot is placed on top of the obstacle and the inside arm is then released, while the outside foot pushes the practitioner off the obstacle.

{{Infobox technique
|image = 
|discipline = [[Freerunning]]
|difficulty = Basic
}}
The '''Scissor Vault''' is a [[vault]] used in [[freerunning]] where the practitioner performs a [[lazy vault]], but instead of just bringing their legs in the air they imitate a running, scissor-kick-like motion with their legs before landing for added style.

{{Infobox technique
|image = 
|discipline = [[Parkour]]
|difficulty = Basic
}}
The '''Shoulder Vault''' is a [[vault]] used in [[parkour]] where the practitioner performs a [[roll|shoulder roll]] over an obstacle. Generally this is done by approaching the obstacles from the side or back and then quickly rolling over it before popping off and landing on their feet.

{{Infobox technique
|image = 
|discipline = [[Parkour]]
|difficulty = Beginner
}}
The '''Side Vault''' (also known as the '''Two-Handed Vault''', '''Basic Vault''' or '''Simple Vault''') is a [[vault]] used in [[parkour]] that is performed by putting both hands on the obstacle on entrance then pushing yourself up with both of your hands and your legs sideways over the object.

{{Infobox technique
|image = 0.jpg
|discipline = [[Freerunning]]
|difficulty = Basic
}}
A '''Star Vault''' is a [[vault]] used in [[freerunning]] where the practitioner does a two-handed [[cartwheel]] over an object.

{{Infobox technique
|image = 
|discipline = [[Freerunning]]
|difficulty = Intermediate
}}
The'''Straddle Vault''' is a [[vault]] used in [[freerunning]] where the practitioner does a [[monkey vault]], but instead of pulling their legs in-between their arms their legs perform a split to the left and right over the obstacle for added style.

{{Infobox technique
|image = 
|discipline = [[Parkour]]
|difficulty = Basic
}}
A '''Swing Vault''', also known as a '''Cradle Vault''', is a [[vault]] used in [[parkour]] where the practioner grabs onto two separate parallel rails and swings over one side of it similar to a [[lazy vault|lazy]] or [[thief vault]].

{{Infobox technique
|image = 
|discipline = [[Freerunning]]
|difficulty = Basic
}}
A '''Vert Vault''' is a [[vault]] used in [[freerunning]] where the practitioners hands are placed in a [[side vault]] fashion and one leg is kicked up over their head.
